 "text"}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HweipQGb1vr1TE9gCGrXTg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WGqXB5TLras33KvRgde9sx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker v3.4.0 errors (downstream payments-api impact) - rolled back to v3.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "After this morning's deploy of payments-worker v3.4.0, the service became unhealthy with an 18% error rate in us-east, us-west and eu-west. payments-api (v5.1.0) also showed an 18% error rate, which is downstream of the worker. payments-worker has been rolled back in all production regions to v3.3.0, its last release that was healthy in production. payments-api was not changed. Next steps: confirm payments-worker and payments-api recover, and find the root cause in v3.4.0.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01RdeKU5Ka2Akp6dUhKgCan9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01X259UN7aVLbWJXvHPt6W5A", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled `payments-worker` back to v3.3.0 and it has recovered. `payments-api` is still failing, though.\n\n- **Rollback:** `payments-worker` went from v3.4.0 back to v3.3.0, its last release that was healthy in production. The change is confirmed in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It's healthy again, and its error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 as a SEV2 against `payments-worker`, and on-call has been paged. It records the bad release, the rollback and the effect on `payments-api`.\n- **Still failing:** `payments-api` is still unhealthy at an 18% error rate on v5.1.0. It may need a few minutes to recover now that the worker is fixed. But if the errors don't drop soon, v5.1.0 itself is probably broken too, since its release history already showed it as degraded.\n\nI haven't touched `payments-api`. If it stays unhealthy, I can roll it back to v5.0.0, its last healthy release, and add that to INC-0001. Since v5.0.0 was healthy in production, that wouldn't need change-manager approval. Should I check again in a few minutes and roll it back if it hasn't recovered?", "type": "text"}]}]}